#. Tag: sgmltag
#: dataref.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "KugarData element"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dataref.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <sgmltag class=\"element\">KugarData</sgmltag> element defines a report's "
"data source. The basic structure is a collection of rows and columns. This "
"document does not define data types and their attributes. The report template "
"defines column data type information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dataref.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The document creator can apply an &XSL; style sheet to an existing document to "
"convert it to this format. If &XSL; is used, the creator can apply custom "
"macros using &XSL; for column calculations, sorting, &etc;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: synopsis
#: dataref.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;!ELEMENT KugarData (Row*)&gt;\n"
"&lt;!ATTLIST KugarData\n"
"        Template      CDATA  #REQUIRED&gt;\n"
"\n"
"&lt;!ELEMENT Row EMPTY&gt;\n"
"&lt;!ATTLIST Row\n"
"        level         CDATA  #REQUIRED\n"
"        col1          CDATA  #IMPLIED\n"
"        col2          CDATA  #IMPLIED\n"
"        ...           CDATA  #IMPLIED\n"
"        coln          CDATA  #IMPLIED&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: dataref.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kugar data element"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dataref.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <sgmltag class=\"element\">KugarData</sgmltag> element contains zero or "
"more <sgmltag class=\"element\">Row</sgmltag> elements. A <sgmltag "
"class=\"element\">Row</sgmltag> must contain one <sgmltag class=\"attribute\">"
"level</sgmltag> attribute with a value corresponding to detail level in the "
"template. Other attributes represent data columns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dataref.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The value of the <sgmltag class=\"attribute\">Template</sgmltag> "
"attribute is the &URL; of the report template used to format the data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: dataref.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Row element"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: dataref.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "Attributes"
msgstr "Atributs"

#. Tag: sgmltag
#: dataref.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "level"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dataref.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The attribute value indicates which detail in the report template is used to "
"display data. Rows can contain various column sets for various levels, so any "
"attribute except <sgmltag class=\"attribute\">level</sgmltag> "
"should be stated as #IMPLIED."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: sgmltag
#: dataref.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dataref.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the attribute is the column name, and uses the format as given in "
"the <sgmltag class=\"element\">KugarData</sgmltag> definition. The attribute "
"name is used in the report template to bind the data to the report fields."
msgstr ""

